TEXT -96 -256 Left 2 ;Problem 1.3 - series resonator, and the mechanical and acoustical resonator with the same behaviour (impedance analogy).
TEXT -96 -224 Left 2 !.param R=10 L=10m C=2u
TEXT 784 -32 Left 2 ;electrical:
TEXT 784 0 Left 2 ;10 ohm, 10 mH, 2 uF  ->  current i = I(Vi), impedance V(vin)/I(Vi)
TEXT 784 288 Left 2 ;mechanical:
TEXT 784 320 Left 2 ;R_M = 10 kg/s, M_M = 10 g, C_M = 2 um/N (k = 0.5 MN/m)  ->  velocity u = I(Vu)
TEXT 784 608 Left 2 ;acoustical:
TEXT 784 640 Left 2 ;R_A = 10 Pa s/m^3, M_A = 10 g/m^4, C_A = 2u m^5/N = 0.2 dm^5/N  ->  U = I(VUa)
TEXT -96 880 Left 2 !.ac dec 1000 10 100k
TEXT -96 928 Left 2 ;Plot I(Vi) and V(vin)/I(Vi): current peaks at f0 = 1/(2 pi sqrt(LC)) = 1125.4 Hz with 1/R = 100 mA, |Z| dips to R = 10 ohm, bandwidth R/(2 pi L) = 159 Hz.
